cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this manuscript or its reproducibility materials, please cite this work."
title: >-
  A Curvature-Deformed Arcsine Coordinate for Cubic Geometric Refinement:
  Exact Spherical Conjugacy, Riemannian Expansion Through Fifth Order, and a
  High-Precision Weight-Six Reconstruction
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Baker"
    given-names: "Wayne"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-08"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A normalized intrinsic geodesic side law defines an exact local linearizing
  coordinate for geometric refinement on a Riemannian surface. The associated
  curvature-deformed arcsine is obtained exactly on the sphere, analytically
  through geometric weight five on general surfaces, and extended at weight
  six by high-precision rational reconstruction with independent holdout tests.
keywords:
  - Riemannian geometry
  - geodesic side law
  - arcsine
  - Schroeder equation
  - Koenigs linearization
  - curvature invariants
  - cubic refinement
  - extrapolation
